.Dd November 10, 2026
.Dt IVSHMEMD 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ivshmemd
.Nd serve QEMU's ivshmem-doorbell a region the kernel's virtio-gpu shares
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl n Ar node
.Op Fl s Ar size
.Ar socket
.Nm
.Op Fl n Ar node
.Fl i
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
makes a sealed memfd of
.Ar size
bytes and four eventfds, attaches them to the kernel through
.Pa /dev/vgpu-shm
.Pq Xr vgpu-shm 4
as peer 0, and listens on the Unix socket
.Ar socket
for one QEMU whose
.Sy ivshmem-doorbell
device has two vectors:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
ivshmemd /tmp/ivs.sock &
qemu-system-x86_64 -accel kvm -machine q35,kernel-irqchip=split ... \e
    -chardev socket,path=/tmp/ivs.sock,id=ivs \e
    -device ivshmem-doorbell,chardev=ivs,vectors=2
.Ed
.Pp
It speaks the server protocol of QEMU's
.Pa docs/specs/ivshmem-spec.rst :
version 0, the id 1 for QEMU, the region, then peer 0's two eventfds,
which the virtual machine rings for the kernel, and peer 1's two, which
the kernel rings to raise the machine's vectors.
The virtual machine runs the virtio-gpu device over the region, and the
kernel binds its driver to it.
.Pp
When QEMU's connection closes,
.Nm
detaches the region as lost, which fails every pending fence; after
.Dv SIGINT
or
.Dv SIGTERM
it detaches in order.
Before the detach it prints the transport's report, and then exits.
.Pp
The options:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl i
Print the transport's report and exit, without attaching.
.It Fl n Ar node
The control node, by default
.Pa /dev/vgpu-shm .
.It Fl s Ar size
The region's size, a power of two from 32K to 64M, with an optional
.Sy K
or
.Sy M ;
by default 32M.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 after the detach or the report, 1 when the region, the attach, the
socket or the node fails, and 2 for a usage error.
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
.Nm
prints
.Ql ivshmemd: attached: 33554432 bytes as peer 0 ,
.Ql ivshmemd: listening on SOCKET
and
.Ql ivshmemd: QEMU connected as peer 1
as it goes, and last
.Ql ivshmemd: result: detached: QEMU closed its connection
or
.Ql in order .
The report is one line,
.Ql ivshmemd: info: attached 1, bound 1, epoch 2, driver 3, device 3, error 0, doorbells 1, binds 1, rung 10/0, woken 9/1, polls 0, heap 7 of 8189 pages, refused 0 ,
which gives
.Vt struct vgs_info
in order.
A second attach while one is held prints
.Ql ivshmemd: attach: refused /dev/vgpu-shm: Device or resource busy .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr qemu-system 1 ,
.Xr eventfd 2 ,
.Xr memfd_create 2 ,
.Xr kvm 4 ,
.Xr vgpu-shm 4
